## Third-Party Components and Data-Flow Disclosure

The standalone prototype uses Python (Python Software Foundation License), FastAPI (MIT), Next.js (MIT), React (MIT), TypeScript (Apache-2.0), Tailwind CSS (MIT), SQLite (public domain), FFmpeg (LGPL or GPL depending on build), and OpenVINO (Apache-2.0). It also uses the OpenVINO Open Model Zoo person-detection-0202 model, subject to its model-specific licence.

ChatGPT assisted with planning and documentation. OpenVINO performs local person detection in the standalone prototype. The proposed UGREEN Skill uses the supported UGOS Surveillance expert workflow and NAS-local AI model where available. No external transfer of surveillance footage or event data is planned.

The standalone application and UGREEN Skill are separate components. NAS integration remains pending validation.